  <model metaid="meta_dextromethorphan_kidney" id="dextromethorphan_kidney" name="Dextromethorphan (DXM) kidney model" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Kidney model of the renal excretion of dextromethorphan</h1>
        <p>The renal clearance of a substance is <code>GFR * fu_&lt;sid&gt; * &lt;X&gt;EX_f</code>, the
filtration of its unbound fraction times a factor: 1 is filtration alone,
above 1 a net tubular secretion, below 1 a net reabsorption. The glomerular
filtration rate is <code>GFR = f_renal_function * GFR_base</code>, <code>GFR_base</code> is 101
ml/min at 75 kg and scales with the renal blood flow; a measured creatinine
clearance of X ml/min is the renal function X/101.</p>
        <p>The factors are of the renal clearances and the urinary recoveries of the
literature: the renal clearance of dextromethorphan in poor metabolizers is
41-78 ml/min (Schadel1995, Capon1996) with 11-26 % of an oral dose excreted
unchanged, extensive metabolizers excrete 0.2 % unchanged and 27-39 % as
total dextrorphan.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
